# FlexYug: Project Conventions

## Architecture

FlexYug is a **mobile-only, local-first** strength-training journal built with Expo + React Native. SQLite on the device is the source of truth during a session; Supabase is a durable mirror reached only by the sync engine. Do not introduce API servers, ORMs, middleware, or server-side rendering. The UI must never block on the network.

The product is **FlexYug**; the repo/directory name `vyayamy` predates the rename and refers only to the repository itself.

## Stack Guardrails

Do NOT replace, remove, or migrate away from any of the following without explicit approval and a documented reason:

- **Expo SDK 56**, **React Native 0.85**, **React 19.2** (no DOM, no web APIs)
- **TypeScript** with `strict: true`
- **Expo Router** (file-based, typed routes) for navigation
- **`expo-sqlite`** as the local source of truth
- **Supabase JS client** talking directly to PostgREST + GoTrue, imported **only** from `src/sync/**` and `src/auth/**` (enforced by `no-restricted-imports`); everything else goes through the auth facade `src/auth/authActions.ts` or the queries layer
- **TanStack React Query 5** for all server state (reads SQLite, not HTTP)
- **`useTheme()` + `useMemo(makeStyles)`** for styling, with tokens from `src/ui/colors.ts` / `typography.ts` / `motion.ts` exposed via `src/ui/useTheme.ts`, and text rendered through the `src/ui/Text.tsx` primitive; no CSS files, no CSS-in-JS (`src/ui/theme.ts` is a deprecated static shim for the boot overlay and `brand` constants only)
- **`react-native-svg`** for charts
- **`expo-haptics`** (via the `src/ui/haptics.ts` wrappers), **`expo-notifications`** for feedback and background rest cues
- **`@sentry/react-native`** for error reporting (gated by `EXPO_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN`)
- **Jest + `ts-jest`** with `better-sqlite3` mocking `expo-sqlite`

Do not add state management libraries (Redux, Zustand, Jotai, etc.). UI state uses `useState`/`useReducer`; server state belongs in React Query.

Do not add Recharts or `victory-native` (React version conflict). Charts are in-house SVG.

## Directory Structure

```
app/                          Expo Router routes (file-based)
  _layout.tsx                 Root stack + providers + db init + sync engine
                              + root auth gate + magic-link deep-link handler
  (tabs)/                     Bottom tabs (today, progress, profile)
  login.tsx, workout/active.tsx,   Stack screens
  history/index.tsx, history/[id].tsx, profile/plan/*

src/
  auth/                       Supabase client singleton, authActions facade, AuthProvider, useAuth
  components/                 Shared presentational components
  core/                       Pure domain logic (PR detection, format, units, sync helpers)
  db/                         SQLite schema, client, enqueueMutation, mutation event bus, uuid, types, mocks
  lib/                        Cross-cutting services (errorReporting, restNotifications, kvStore)
  queries/                    React Query hooks reading SQLite, one file per domain
  screens/                    Large screens imported by app/ routes
  sync/                       engine.ts, push.ts, pull.ts, state.ts, quarantine.ts, outboxPreview.ts
  ui/                         useTheme, skins, Text primitive, charts, haptics, error boundary
  voice/                      Voice logging (grammar, commands, dispatch, speech engine)
  __tests__/                  Integration tests

supabase/
  migrations/                 Numbered SQL migrations
  seed.sql                    Global exercise library
```

Preserve this layout. New features fit into the existing directories. Do not restructure, flatten, or introduce barrel files (`index.ts` re-exports).

## File Naming

| Kind                | Convention  | Example                    |
| ------------------- | ----------- | -------------------------- |
| Screens/components  | PascalCase  | `ExerciseBlock.tsx`        |
| Route files         | lowercase   | `today.tsx`, `[id].tsx`    |
| Query modules       | camelCase   | `workouts.ts`, `sets.ts`   |
| Lib/utility files   | camelCase   | `errorReporting.ts`        |
| Type files          | camelCase   | `types.ts`                 |

## Import Order

1. React / React hooks
2. React Native primitives (`View`, `Text`, `Pressable`, ...)
3. Third-party packages (Expo, TanStack Query, Supabase, Sentry, ...)
4. Internal modules via `@/` alias (`@/db`, `@/sync`, `@/ui`, ...)
5. Type-only imports use `import type { ... }`

No CSS imports; styles are co-located in the component file via a `makeStyles(theme)` factory.

## Provider Tree (do not reorder)

Defined in `app/_layout.tsx`:

```
ErrorBoundary → GestureHandlerRootView → SafeAreaProvider → SkinProvider →
  QueryClientProvider → AuthProvider → ToastProvider → <Stack> (+ BootOverlay)
```

`RootLayout` races `initDb()` against a timeout, then calls `startSyncEngine(queryClient)`. The Stack renders immediately; a boot overlay covers it until the db, fonts, and skin hydration are ready. The root layout also owns the magic-link deep-link handler (`exchangeCodeForSession`) and the single root-level auth gate that redirects any non-login route to `/login` when there is no session (do not add per-route guards).

## Cross-cutting Rules

- UI code must not call `supabase.from(...)`. Only `src/sync/**` and `src/auth/**` may import `@/auth/supabase` (lint-enforced via `no-restricted-imports`); screens use the facade `src/auth/authActions.ts`.
- Every read query must filter `deleted_at IS NULL`. Tombstones are for the sync engine.
- Every mutation must go through `enqueueMutation` in `src/db/mutations.ts`. Committed writes emit on the mutation event bus (`src/db/mutationEvents.ts`); the sync engine subscribes and debounces a push, so query code never imports the sync engine.
- New synced tables must be added to `SYNCED_TABLES` in `src/db/schema.ts` AND have `updated_at` + `deleted_at` in their Postgres migration. `personal_records` is intentionally NOT synced; it is a local derived cache recomputed from `sets`.
